{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You came in tonight because of some cough and nausea, but we also noticed your oxygen levels dropped while you were sleeping. Can you tell me more about how you’ve been feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I had a bit of a cough and felt kind of sick, but nothing too bad. I didn’t think I needed to come in, but they said my blood pressure was high and my oxygen was low when I was asleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Your oxygen dipped below normal while you were resting, which is concerning. You mentioned you have sleep apnea—have you been using your CPAP machine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I tried it years ago, but it made me uncomfortable. I haven’t used it since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that might explain the low oxygen. A recent sleep study suggested you may have complex sleep apnea, where CPAP can sometimes make breathing pauses worse. The sleep specialist recommends trying oxygen at night instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oxygen? Like a nasal cannula? I’ve used that before. I think I can handle that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We’re arranging for home oxygen—3 liters per minute at night. It’ll be delivered to your house tomorrow before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better than the CPAP mask. Will I need it forever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2153-11-18 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll need to follow up with another supervised sleep study as an outpatient to be sure. For now, this should help keep your oxygen levels stable at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2153-11-18 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also checked your kidney function and transplant. Everything looks stable—your creatinine is about the same as usual, and your tacrolimus level is in the right range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2153-11-18 21:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been taking my meds regularly, except yesterday I forgot because I was nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2153-11-18 21:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. We gave you your usual medications here, including your insulin, blood pressure pills, and tacrolimus. Your blood pressure has come down nicely since you got here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2153-11-18 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had high BP on and off. My nephrologist was thinking about adding another med."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2153-11-18 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked a serum renin level today to help evaluate the cause. Your outpatient team will review that and decide if any changes are needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning look stable. Your oxygen was 95% on room air while awake, and your kidney and diabetes markers haven’t changed much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you later today. Your back pain is better with the lidocaine patch and Tylenol, and your cough is improving. The main thing is setting up your nighttime oxygen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds? I want to make sure I’m not missing anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on all your usual medications. We’ve updated your list—nothing new except the oxygen at night. A nurse will go over everything with you before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot and hand? They’ve been dry and cold, but no new pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2153-11-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your amputation sites are healing well, and your circulation is stable for now. Continue with your aspirin and statin, and keep following up with your vascular doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2153-11-19 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The oxygen supplier confirmed delivery to your home this afternoon. Once it arrives, start using it at night as prescribed—3 liters via nasal cannula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2153-11-19 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll see my sleep doctor soon for the next test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2153-11-19 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll schedule a supervised sleep study as an outpatient. Also, your nephrologist will follow up on the renin test and your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2153-11-19 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Everything’s ready for discharge. You’re doing well—oxygen stable, no fever, and you’re able to walk independently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2153-11-19 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I’m glad it wasn’t anything more serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2153-11-19 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Just remember to use the oxygen at night, take your meds, and keep your follow-up appointments. Call if you have any trouble breathing or new symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2153-11-19 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2153-11-18 20:16:00",
    "admission_end": "2153-11-19 17:44:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with a history of type 2 diabetes, end-stage renal disease status post kidney transplant, peripheral vascular disease with prior amputations, and obstructive sleep apnea was admitted for cough, nausea, and nocturnal hypoxia. His blood pressure was elevated on presentation but improved with medication. He was found to have oxygen desaturation during sleep, consistent with his known sleep apnea, which he had not been treating due to CPAP discomfort. A plan was made with the sleep team to initiate nocturnal home oxygen at 3 liters per minute instead of PAP therapy, given concern for complex sleep apnea. His kidney function remained stable, tacrolimus levels were therapeutic, and his other chronic conditions were managed without change. He was discharged home the following day with arranged oxygen delivery and plans for outpatient follow-up with sleep and nephrology specialists.",
    "problems": [
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Kidney transplant status",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease with stage 5 chronic kidney disease or end stage renal disease",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic peripheral angiopathy with gangrene",
      "Gangrene, not elsewhere classified",
      "Hypoxemia",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Acquired absence of left leg below knee",
      "Acquired absence of other right toe(s)",
      "Acquired absence of right finger(s)",
      "Dorsalgia, unspecified",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic nephropathy",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic chronic kidney disease"
    ]
  }
}
